  "summary": "Ten years in technology will sharpen you in ways a job title never captures.\n \nI started in software engineering and never stopped, but what defines my career isn't the code I've written, it's the programs I've driven, the teams I've aligned, and the outcomes I've delivered. At ELLKAY, I've worn more hats than my title suggests: owning cross-functional roadmaps, navigating stakeholders, and building the kind of operational discipline that turns ambiguous problems into measurable results.\n \nBeyond my day job, I build. Early-stage ventures have taught me what enterprise experience sometimes can't, how to move fast, make decisions with incomplete information, and bet on your own judgment.\n \nI'm drawn to roles at the intersection of technology, strategy, and execution, where the work is hard, the stakes are real, and clarity is the most valuable thing you can create. Open to connecting across enterprise SaaS, AI platforms, fintech, and beyond.",
